IBdebuglog.txt

# Dropped-in server forensic segments for analysis (not repo content)
*.jsonl.log
guardiant.log

# The archive companion to the above. 42.20's write-extension allowlist renamed
# Memoir's recovery point from "latest.json" to "latest.json.txt" (RDShared
# .EXT_DOC), and no rule here followed it - so a pulled archive sat untracked and
# committable while its sibling events log was correctly ignored. These carry a
# named player's full character: username, life ids, every skill and trait.
# Caught 2026-08-09 with Mox's snapshot one `git add -A` away from going public.
*.json.txt

# Generated forensic reports - rebuild with tools/forensic-report.py, never commit
# (a single run embeds the whole ring: ~1.9MB for 3.6k records)
*forensic-report.html

# --- RFTDEchoes binary assets: forked from Wasteland Musicians, NOT in git ---
# 129.9MB of .ogg plus the .fbx anims - permanent history bloat for files that
# are never hand-edited, and third-party audio we do not republish. The payload
# folder and the Mosaic copy carry them; git carries the code that drives them.
# CONSEQUENCE: git is NOT a complete backup of the payload. Keep a second copy
# of RFTDEchoes\42\media\sound before anything destructive (see 2026-08-02).
RequiemOfTheDead/Contents/mods/RFTDEchoes/42/media/sound/
RequiemOfTheDead/Contents/mods/RFTDEchoes/42/media/anims_X/

# --- Bug-hunt working set: pulled server logs and the files under review ---
# Same rule as netprobe captures. bughuntresults/remote and wireremotetest.log
# are raw dedi output carrying steam-ids, IPs and usernames; the .lua copies in
# there are snapshots of files that already live in the tree. Nothing here is
# repo content, and one of them is 2.3MB of live player data.
bughuntresults/

# --- Design/engine documentation: local-only, purged from history 2026-08-09 ---
# The docs/ tree is working notes, engine teardowns and legacy Workshop items -
# 9.4MB that was never meant to be public. Removed from GitHub and from every
# commit that carried it (git filter-repo), and kept out from here on.
# NOTE: this must be `docs/*`, not `docs/`. Git does not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so a `!` exception under `docs/` would never re-include -
# and the one file below is a live test fixture that has to stay tracked.
docs/*

# The Limes import fixture: test_lmimport.lua and test_lmpersist.lua parse this
# file directly and os.exit(2) without it. It is test data, not documentation,
# so it survives the purge and stays in git.
!docs/dirge-phunzones.md

# --- Native DLL decompiles: reference only, regenerate with Ghidra headless ---
PZ_Natives_Decompiled_*/
